2) can a model learn what a passage is worth without opening it?
                                 rows   cvs  pearson    rho    auc  mean abs err  base rate  alpha
value model, held out CV by CV  666.0  33.0    0.806  0.787  0.926         0.107      0.128   0.01
   feature weights: similarity +5.594, rank within requirement -0.030, similarity z-score +0.032, position in CV -0.006, passage share of CV -0.023, requirement index -0.242
   base rate: a passage answers a requirement outright 12.8% of the time, so chance would be an AUC of 0.5.
   the signal is in one feature: similarity carries it and the geometry features sit near zero, which is why a passage that answers a requirement can be picked out of an unseen CV's candidate list 92.6% of the time without opening it.

